<noscript><p class="note">Interactive tools need JavaScript. The power table, pin map and <a href="?page=manual">full manual</a> remain available.</p></noscript>
<section id="power" class="content"><h2>Choose the power state</h2><p>Explanatory checklist only. The teacher must validate the actual modules and power arrangement.</p><label class="js-only">Activity <select id="power-state"><option value="all">Show all states</option><option value="upload">Upload</option><option value="diagnostic">USB diagnostic</option><option value="motor">USB motor test</option><option value="battery">Battery run</option><option value="change">Change wiring</option></select></label><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>USB and external power must not be combined without teacher validation.</caption><thead><tr><th>Activity</th><th>USB</th><th>Motor battery</th><th>External ESP32 5 V</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<?php foreach([
 ['upload','Upload','Connected','OFF','Disconnected / teacher isolated'],['diagnostic','USB diagnostic','Connected','OFF','Disconnected / teacher isolated'],['motor','USB motor test','Connected only after teacher approval','ON only after teacher approval; wheels raised','Isolated from ESP32; exact circuit checked; common ground'],['battery','Battery run','Unplugged','Teacher turns ON after checks','Connected only after regulator validation'],['change','Change wiring','Unplugged','OFF; cells disconnected for assembly','Never change a live lead']
] as $row):?><tr data-power="<?=$row[0]?>"><?php foreach(array_slice($row,1) as $cell):?><td><?=e($cell)?></td><?php endforeach ?></tr><?php endforeach ?></tbody></table></div><p>If USB motor power is not approved, pair Bluetooth with motors OFF and use the teacher-approved battery-only test. If neither works, ask the teacher. <a href="?page=lesson&amp;slug=wiring">Read the full power procedure</a>.</p></section>
<section id="wiring" class="content"><h2>Trace a signal</h2><p><strong>Provisional logical schematic — not physical pin placement.</strong> Read actual board labels with the teacher. ENA/ENB PWM jumpers are separate from regulator 5V-EN.</p><label class="js-only">Mode <select id="wire-mode"><option value="base">Base / remote</option><option value="line">Line</option><option value="obstacle">Obstacle</option></select></label><div class="wire-diagram" aria-live="polite"><strong id="wire-from">ESP32 GPIO25</strong><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><strong id="wire-to">L298N IN1</strong></div><p id="wire-role">3.3 V logic signal · motor direction. Not a motor power connection.</p><div class="page-tools js-only"><button type="button" id="wire-zoom">Enlarge connection</button></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Configured GPIO map · no physical pin order implied</caption><thead><tr><th>Connection</th><th>GPIO</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach(require $root.'/config/robots.php' as $label=>$pin):$sensor=str_contains($label,'_IR');$role=$sensor?'Driven 3.3 V digital sensor OUT; VCC only on confirmed 3V3, GND common':(str_starts_with($label,'EN')?'3.3 V PWM logic; remove only the matching motor-enable jumper':'3.3 V direction logic; not motor power');?><tr data-wire-kind="<?=$sensor?($label==='FRONT_IR'?'front':'sensor'):'base'?>"><td><button type="button" class="secondary" data-wire="<?=e($label)?>" data-pin="<?=$pin?>" data-role="<?=e($role)?>"><?=e($label)?></button></td><td><?=$pin?></td><td><?=e($role)?></td></tr><?php endforeach ?></tbody></table></div><p>GPIO34/35/39 have no internal pull-ups. A disconnected sensor may float. No 5 V signal on GPIO. <a href="?page=lesson&amp;slug=wiring">Power and motor-output connections</a>.</p></section>
<section id="calibration" class="content"><h2>Record what your sensors see</h2><p>Motor battery OFF, USB diagnostic power only, external 5 V isolated. Use the <a href="?page=download&amp;file=00_Sensor_Check">sensor diagnostic sketch</a>. Record black versus white for line mode, obstacle versus clear for avoidance.</p><form id="calibration-form"><label>Mode <select name="mode"><option value="line">Two downward line sensors</option><option value="obstacle">Three obstacle sensors</option></select></label><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Measured raw digital levels</caption><thead><tr><th>Sensor</th><th>Detected (black / obstacle)</th><th>Clear (white / no obstacle)</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach(['left','front','right'] as $sensor):?><tr><th><?=ucfirst($sensor)?></th><?php foreach(['detected','clear'] as $state):?><td><select aria-label="<?=$sensor.' '.$state?>" name="<?=$sensor.'_'.$state?>"><option value="">Not measured</option><option>LOW</option><option>HIGH</option><option value="unstable">Unstable / disconnected</option></select></td><?php endforeach ?></tr><?php endforeach ?></tbody></table></div><label>Surface, lighting &amp; measured height / distance <input name="conditions" maxlength="240"></label><label>Motor inversion notes <input name="inversion" maxlength="160" placeholder="Record measured LEFT and RIGHT settings"></label><div class="page-tools js-only"><button type="submit">Interpret readings</button><button type="button" id="save-calibration" class="secondary">Save on this device</button><button type="button" id="export-calibration" class="secondary">Export notes</button><button type="reset" class="secondary">Clear readings</button></div></form><p id="calibration-result" role="status">No recommendation until all required sensors have two stable, opposite readings. Front is unused in line mode.</p><p>Mixed polarities cannot use the existing single DETECTED_LEVEL. Ask the teacher; a global inversion cannot fix mixed modules.</p><button type="button" data-print class="js-only">Print worksheet</button></section>
<section id="troubleshooter" class="content"><h2>Find the next check</h2><p>Stop motion before investigating. Do not change live wiring or keep retrying a jammed motor.</p><div id="trouble-question" aria-live="polite"></div><div id="trouble-options" class="page-tools"></div><button type="button" id="trouble-back" class="secondary js-only">Back</button><a href="?page=lesson&amp;slug=troubleshooting#tell-the-teacher-these-five-facts">Ask my teacher / I don’t know</a><p><a href="?page=lesson&amp;slug=troubleshooting">Read all symptoms and fixes</a></p></section>
<section id="serial-practice" class="content"><h2>Serial Monitor practice</h2><p class="warning"><strong>SIMULATION — no robot connected.</strong> No USB or Bluetooth connection is opened. This does not test your hardware.</p><form id="serial-form"><label>Simulated sketch <select id="sim-sketch"><option value="usb">00_Serial_Test</option><option value="remote">01_Remote_Control</option></select></label><label>Baud <select id="sim-baud"><option>115200</option><option>9600</option></select></label><label>Line ending <select id="sim-ending"><option value="newline">Newline</option><option value="none">No line ending</option><option value="both">Both NL &amp; CR</option></select></label><label>Command <input id="sim-command" maxlength="32" autocomplete="off" value="PING"></label><button>Send simulated command</button><button type="button" id="serial-reset" class="secondary">Reset</button></form><pre id="serial-output" role="status">Ready. Send PING with Newline.</pre><p id="serial-timer">Virtual wheels: stopped</p><p>The USB diagnostic waits up to 200 ms without a newline; remote commands are individual uppercase characters and ignore line endings. Remote motion stops after 800 ms without another movement command.</p></section>
<section id="decisions" class="content"><h2>Explore sensor decisions</h2><p class="warning"><strong>SIMULATION — no robot connected.</strong> Detected means calibrated black / obstacle. Timing mirrors the shipped firmware, not measured movement.</p><label>Mode <select id="decision-mode"><option value="line">Line follower</option><option value="obstacle">Obstacle avoidance</option></select></label><fieldset><legend>Detected inputs</legend><?php foreach(['left','front','right'] as $sensor):?><label><input type="checkbox" id="detect-<?=$sensor?>"> <?=ucfirst($sensor)?></label><?php endforeach ?></fieldset><div class="page-tools"><button id="decision-play" type="button">Play</button><button id="decision-pause" type="button">Pause</button><button id="decision-step" type="button">Step 50 ms</button><button id="decision-reset" type="button">Reset session</button><label>Speed <select id="decision-speed"><option value="1">1×</option><option value="0.25">¼×</option><option value="2">2×</option></select></label></div><div class="wire-diagram"><span id="left-wheel">Left: stopped</span><span aria-hidden="true">↑ front</span><span id="right-wheel">Right: stopped</span></div><p id="decision-output" role="status"></p><p>Line: both white is ambiguous: forward 700 ms, search 1,500 ms, then latched stop. Both black latches stop. Obstacle: front clear goes forward; front blocked chooses left if clear, else right if clear; all blocked reverses 350 ms then turns left 800 ms. A normal turn lasts 400 ms. No rear sensing. Both sessions stop at 60 s; Reset starts a new simulated session.</p><a href="?page=lesson&amp;slug=line">Line instructions</a> · <a href="?page=lesson&amp;slug=obstacle">Obstacle instructions</a></section>
